  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 as RNA encoder dramatically outperforms scgpt (~20% gap), and among scvi_n200+imagenet_vit_l configs, transformer aggregation with concat fusion is best (0.7207, config_009), though the margin over avgpool+concat (0.7150) is small. The image encoder (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) has not been tested with scvi_n200, which is the critical unexplored axis. This experiment (config_030: scvi_n200 + resnet50, transformer, concat) tests whether a different image encoder can match or exceed imagenet_vit_l under the best aggregation/fusion settings. It is the best use of experiment 6 because it isolates the image-encoder variable while holding the top-performing RNA encoder, aggregation, and fusion fixed, reducing uncertainty about whether the current 0.72 ceiling is due to the image encoder or the overall architecture. With 4 experiments remaining after this, the result will guide whether to exploit the imagenet_vit_l direction further or pivot to resnet50 variants."
}

